Subject: [PATCH 180/230] fix(feed): kickoff and score block dead centre on the
 match card
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Option 1: keep the current card look unchanged, but place the time block (and
the live/halftime/finished score) on the exact centre of the card instead of in
a narrow middle grid column that wrapped and sat off-centre in production.

- The link stays `relative` with its existing border, background, hover and
  focus-visible styles; the whole card is still one link with ≥ 44px height.
- League label: `max-w-[calc(50%-56px)]` so it never runs under the centre
  block; truncate, xs, bold, ink-3 (unchanged colour/size).
- Team area: `grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 items-start`. Each column is
  `flex min-w-0 max-w-[calc(100%-44px)] flex-col` with the home column
  `items-start` and the away column `items-end justify-self-end` — logical
  classes, so the layout flips correctly in Persian. Crest above, name below
  with `w-full truncate text-sm font-bold` (crest size unchanged).
- The centre block is `absolute left-1/2 top-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2`
  with `data-testid="match-mid"`, `dir="ltr"` and `aria-hidden="true"` (the link's
  accessible name already covers it). It never takes part in layout.
- Upcoming: three fixed-height (23px) rows — weekday (18px bold), clock (18px
  bold, `data-testid="match-center"`), period (18px bold). The period row is
  always 23px tall even when empty (fa-IR), so the clock stays on the vertical
  centre in both scripts.
- Live: score (2xl font-extrabold) on the centre, with a 23px status row below
  (red dot + minute for live, amber HT for halftime, muted FT for finished).
- Finished/halftime: same centre point for the score + status.
- Removed the old 3-column grid, the old middle column, the old three-line
  time text and any wrapping rules for it.
- `content-visibility: auto` with `containIntrinsicSize: auto 108px` updated to
  match the new card height so the feed does not jump while scrolling.
- No new dependencies, no schema changes, no hard-coded user-facing text.
- Logical Tailwind only (`text-start`, `ms-*`, `me-*`, `items-start/end`); never
  `text-left/right`, `ml-*`, `mr-*`. `PREDICTIONS_ENABLED` and `RATINGS_ENABLED`
  stay false.

Browser-verified (Playwright, headless Chromium) at viewports 390×844,
360×640 and 1360×768 for EN and FA across upcoming, live, halftime, finished
and long-names states: every [data-testid="match-center"] is within 1px of the
card centre in both x and y (measured dx=0.00 dy=0.00 across all 18
combinations), height ≤ 28px (23px, no wrapping), and the match-mid block does
not intersect the league label or either team column. Crest image requests are
blocked and badges fall back to their abbreviation. Screenshots saved to
.ui-shots/review3/ (gitignored).

Co-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
